gametitle=Champions: Return to Arms (SLUS-20973) v2.00

[Net test: cutscene audio sync off]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Stops cutscenes from nudging the speaking character's animation clock toward the local audio stream position (cut_advance, 0x199448). Cosmetic effect: lip movement may drift from the voice line. Every player in a game must use the same setting.
patch=1,EE,00199448,word,10000060

[Net test: prediction copy starts without pending damage]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Each machine predicts its own player on a throwaway copy. The copy is cloned with any damage still waiting on the real player, can die from it during prediction, and its death rebuilds the alive-player list on that one machine (FINDINGS G11-G18). This makes the clone start with no pending damage (Player_clone, 0x11EA8C), so the copy never dies ahead of the real player. Real deaths are untouched. Per machine; does not need to match between players. Replaces an earlier test patch at 0x1B3504, withdrawn because it changed real deaths (G21).
// was: E60000C8 (swc1 f0,0xc8(s0))  now: sw zero,0xc8(s0)
patch=1,EE,0011EA8C,word,AE0000C8

[Net test: input delay drains faster]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=After a stall the game keeps the extra input delay and gives it back one frame per 62 calls, or per 31 calls when this machine is well behind its peers (net_main, 0x133574 and 0x1335C0). This shortens both windows to 12 and 8 calls. Pacing is per machine and does not change what the simulation computes, but a machine that holds a call can make the others wait for its input. FINDINGS L4.
// was: 2862001F (slti v0,v1,31) / 2863003D (slti v1,v1,61)
patch=1,EE,00133574,word,28620008
patch=1,EE,001335C0,word,2863000B

[Net test: lower input delay cap]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=The game stops sampling input once it is 38 frames (about 0.6 s) ahead of the slowest simulation; this lowers the cap to 14 frames. Trades long input lag for more visible pauses. FINDINGS L4.
// was: 28420027 (slti v0,v0,39)
patch=1,EE,00133554,word,2842000F

[Arena diagnostic: knight never summons]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Diagnostic only, changes the fight. The fourth knight of the Drundar arena never casts Summon Skeleton (Horsemen_run, 0x2726F4). If the arena still goes out of sync with this on every machine, the skeletons are not involved. Every player must use the same setting.
// was: 1462000D (bne v1,v0,+13)
patch=1,EE,002726F4,word,1000000D

[Arena diagnostic: pool reaper off]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Diagnostic only. The low-memory reaper never deletes expendable objects (runObjects, 0x14B9CC). If the object pool really runs low, new objects silently fail to appear. Tests FINDINGS D21. Every player must use the same setting.
// was: 2842012C (slti v0,v0,300)
patch=1,EE,0014B9CC,word,28420000

[Arena diagnostic: generic talk animation in cutscenes]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Diagnostic only. Cutscene speakers always use the generic talk loop instead of the per-line lip-sync animation, which also stops the audio-driven animation nudge (cut_execKey, 0x196AA0). Lips no longer follow the voice. Tests FINDINGS D8 and engine P6. Every player should use the same setting.
// was: 0062102A (slt v0,v1,v0)
patch=1,EE,00196AA0,word,00001021

[Arena diagnostic: never judge activity from the camera]
author=reverse engineering test patch, untested on a running game
description=Diagnostic only. In a net game object activity is always judged from player positions, never from the cutscene camera (gameSetObjectVis, 0x1E4DD4). Scenery far from the players stops animating during cutscenes. Tests FINDINGS D6. Every player must use the same setting.
// was: 8043FCD0 (lb v1,-0x330(v0))
patch=1,EE,001E4DD4,word,00001821
